  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 65570,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/stephanstapel/BrickStoreSharp",
  "published": "2026-10-28T06:17:47.62Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.2.0\nNew\n* Targets .NET Standard 2.0, .NET 8 and .NET 10\n* New item properties Reserved, Cost, TotalWeight, MarkerText and MarkerColor\n* Elements not interpreted by the library (e.g. DifferenceBaseValues, GuiState) are kept in AdditionalElements and written back unchanged\n* Item types unknown to the library are written back unchanged\n* Inventory comment is read back when loading\n* Faster loading: each item is read in a single pass\n\nFixed\n* Endless recursion when loading from a stream\n* File handles not being released after loading\n* Prices of 1000 and more were written in a corrupted format; numbers are now written culture-invariant and without rounding\n* Status, condition, item type and sub condition are written as BrickStore codes (I/X/E, N/U, ...)\n* Currency and BrickLinkChangelogId are read and written as attributes of <Inventory>\n* Category, comments, retain, bulk, sale, stockroom, sub condition and tiered prices are no longer lost on save/load\n* Default values and empty elements are no longer written\n* Saving to a file writes a temporary file first, an existing file is never destroyed by a failed save\n* Invalid XML characters throw on save instead of producing unreadable files\n* External entities are never resolved when loading (XXE)\n\nBreaking changes\n* Synchronous Load/Save throw the original exception instead of an AggregateException\n* Missing text elements load as null instead of an empty string\n* Items without color are written with ColorID 0 (BrickLink's 'Not Applicable'), as ColorID is required by BrickStore\n\n1.1.0\n* More complete mapping of item fields, type safety enhancements and bug fixes\n\n1.0.0\n* Initial version",
